  "title": "wsutil: Treat vertical tab as whitespace",
  "description": "For some reason glib does not treat all of the standard white-space\ncharacters in the C locale as whitespace, despite the ISO C\nstandard. Specifically, both g_ascii_isspace() and g_unichar_isspace\nreturn FALSE for the vertical tab. This is an intentional decision\nwith the offered reasoning:\n\"the vertical tab is univerally not used, and people won't expect it\nto get passed by these functions and won't be able to handle it.\"\n( https://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=59388 )\n\nWe do expect to replace vertical tab with a space, as with other\nwhitespace characters, in functions like format_text_wsp and\nformat_text_chr. Define our own functions that aren't arbitrarily broken.",
